        "sha": "d5d468a29a2db4c0676c57d60bc8431ed4fd6e18",
        "bucket": "behavior-semantic",
        "subject": "fix(material/autocomplete): clear previous selection on reactive form reset (#27653)",
        "final_disposition": "already-adapted",
        "reason": "The complete two-file/two-hunk reactive-reset change is present in the owned legacy trigger. Programmatic null or undefined clears the previous selected option quietly through the owned value-assignment path. The later null-only condition is retained: zero, false, empty string and an empty display result must not be treated as a missing model. The original intermediate falsy-display guard is therefore not copied. The strengthened existing native reset test first selects an actual option, then requires silent selected-state cleanup and exactly one null CVA write. Current whole-method Forms/RxJS diagnostics support this source judgment; actual Angular DI/rendering, packed behavior and runtime/compiler/RxJS/peer floors remain separate mandatory executions.",
